# {{project_name}}

A self-hosted website-to-RAG chatbot, scaffolded by `web2rag` plugin v{{plugin_version}} on {{generated_at}}.

## Architecture (one diagram)

```
┌────────────────── docker compose (2 services) ────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                            │
│   chroma  ──persists──▶ ./data/chroma                                     │
│                                                                            │
│   api (FastAPI, port 8787)                                                │
│     ├─ in-process: BGE-M3 + bge-reranker-v2-m3 + Prompt-Guard-2 + Detoxify│
│     │              + Presidio  (free, MIT/Apache, baked into image)       │
│     │                                                                      │
│     ├─ POST /ingest   scraper ─▶ guard_ingest ─▶ chunker ─▶ embed ─▶ chroma│
│     ├─ POST /chat     msg ─▶ guard_query ─▶ retrieval ─▶ Claude ─▶        │
│     │                       guard_output ─▶ SSE stream                     │
│     ├─ GET  /widget.js, /widget.css                                       │
│     └─ POST /audit    deepeval + ragas + deepteam runners                 │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Cost contract (hard requirement)

| Phase | Provider | Cost |
|---|---|---|
| Ingest (scrape → guard_ingest → chunk → embed → store) | All in-process: Crawl4AI + Prompt-Guard-2 + Presidio + BGE-M3 + Chroma | **$0** |
| Chat (guard_query → retrieval → LLM → guard_output → SSE) | Claude via Anthropic Console — `CHAT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6` or `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` in `.env` | paid (Anthropic only) |
| Audit / eval (DeepEval correctness+capability + DeepTeam security) | Switchable judge: `--judge anthropic-haiku` or `--judge ollama:<model>` (remote `OLLAMA_URL`) | paid |

**Anything that would charge during ingest is a bug.** This is not a soft preference; the api enforces it.

## 3-guard architecture (free by default)

| Guard | Position | Tools | Goal |
|---|---|---|---|
| `guard_ingest` | per scraped page, before chunking | Prompt-Guard-2 + Presidio + size/type filter + cross-site-link strip | stop attacker-planted instructions and PII from poisoning the corpus |
| `guard_query` | per chat message, before retrieval | Prompt-Guard-2 + Presidio + topic-scope cosine-vs-site-centroid + token-bucket rate limit | stop direct jailbreaks, scope drift, user-side PII leaks |
| `guard_output` | post-LLM, before SSE flush | per-sentence faithfulness vs retrieved chunks (BGE-M3 cosine) + Detoxify + Presidio + citation integrity | catch hallucinations, toxic output, PII leaks, fake citations |

Each returns `GuardResult { passed, severity: low|med|high, reasons[], redacted_text? }`. Severity ≥ high rejects the request; low/med logs and continues. The SSE `done` event includes a `guards` field so the widget can render a "moderated" badge and the audit can replay decisions.

`GUARD_MODE=llm` in `.env` opts every guard into a paid Haiku second-pass for stricter checks.

## Bilingual EN + ID

- BGE-M3 is multilingual (100+ languages) — the same vector space serves both English and Bahasa Indonesia. Cross-lingual retrieval works (Indonesian question → English source chunks → Indonesian answer).
- Widget UI strings live in `widget/src/i18n/{en.json,id.json}`. Locale resolves at runtime: `data-locale="id"` > `navigator.language` > `en`.
- Chat system prompt instructs the LLM to mirror the user's question language. Citations always link to the source URL regardless of language.

## Politeness controls (operator-tunable)

Defaults are polite. Every switch can be overridden in `.env` or per-`/web2rag-ingest` call.

| Knob | `.env` | CLI flag | Default |
|---|---|---|---|
| Honor robots.txt + `noindex`? | `RESPECT_ROBOTS_TXT` | `--force` (set false) | `true` |
| Rate limit | `CRAWL_RATE_LIMIT` | `--rate N/<window>` | `10/60s` |
| Max parallel fetches | `CRAWL_CONCURRENCY` | `--concurrency N` | `2` |
| User-Agent | `CRAWL_USER_AGENT` | `--user-agent "..."` | modern Chrome UA |

Override decisions are recorded in `reports/audit_<ts>.json` with the operator identity so intent stays traceable.

